ve only half a gig  of memory inside them and that is not  good because the Apple eat up all of  your available memory and the OS will  step in and mercy kill the app now iOS  supports virtual memory every computer  operating system now supports virtual  memory but what it doesn't support is it  doesn't support swap so once the system  starts running out of memory starts  mercy killing applications including the  front one most one none of these devices  are in production anymore you can still  use the app on the device but you should  only use it to manage files that are not  notebooks now you might want an Apple  watch if you have the iphone version of  the app you can and you have an Apple  watch you can view your deployments on  the cloud on your Apple watch and I'll  go into how you can do that a little bit  later we will not run your battery all  the way through because the kernel runs  on the cloud side so if you run a  particularly large evaluation we're not  going to blow through all your batteries  here are some of the things that you can  do with the cloud app you can connect to  our cloud or your organization's private  cloud you can browse files and folders  in the cloud space you can create new  notebooks if your plan allows you to  create new notebooks you can edit your  existing notebooks inside our JavaScript  front and anything that you can do in  the cloud on your web desktop web  browser will also work inside the app  you can fill out instant API is instant  web forms you can magnify what you're  looking at you can copy and paste text  from other iOS applications you will be  able to copy and paste images as well in  the next version of the app and I will  show you that as well you can insert  images from the camera or a photo  gallery into  book or a web form you can rename and  delete your cloud objects and you can  also use the app to browse the online  we're from documentation there are some  things you cannot do in the cloud app  you cannot 